## Deployment and config [12-Factor](https://12factor.net/)

> **Examples:** `../examples/twelve-factor.md`

- Store infrastructure config (database URLs, API keys, ports) in environment variables, not hard-coded values.
- Keep `.env*` files empty except for comments; inject real values via environment at runtime.
- Use Symfony secrets or env vars for sensitive values; keep application-behavior parameters in `config/services.yaml` with an `app.` prefix.
- Use constants to define options that rarely change.
- Design processes as stateless; persist durable state in backing services (database, cache, queue), not local filesystem or in-memory globals.
- Treat backing services (DB, mail, cache) as attached resources swappable via config without code changes.
- Treat logs as event streams — write structured logs to stdout/stderr via Monolog; never use `dump()` or `var_dump()` in production paths.
- Run admin and maintenance tasks as one-off console processes (`bin/console`), not as long-lived web requests.
- Maintain dev/prod parity for dependencies, config keys, and backing services.
- Strictly separate build, release, and run stages — compile assets and install dependencies at build time; inject config at release/run time.
